---
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL, DISCLOSURE } from '@config/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} labels affiliate links and separates potential commissions from editorial work.`}
  effectiveDate={LEGAL.effectiveDate}
  lastUpdated={LEGAL.lastUpdated}
>
  <p class="lead">{DISCLOSURE.long}</p>

  <h2 id="how-links-are-labelled">1. How links are labelled</h2>
  <p>
    Where StackPipeline uses a tracked affiliate link, the page includes a clear affiliate
    disclosure near the recommendation and the link is marked for search engines as sponsored.
    A standard vendor or documentation link is not necessarily an affiliate link.
  </p>

  <h2 id="editorial-separation">2. Editorial separation</h2>
  <p>
    Potential compensation should not determine whether a product is covered, its score, its
    rank, or the language of an editorial recommendation. The publication standard is described
    in the <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="current-status">3. Current publisher status</h2>
  <p>
    StackPipeline currently uses an organization-level byline and has not published a verified
    legal entity, public contact channel or display-advertising publisher ID. This disclosure
    describes the intended treatment of qualifying links; it does not represent that every
    outbound vendor link pays a commission.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-cost">4. Your cost</h2>
  <p>
    If a qualifying link generates a commission, it should not change the price you pay to the
    vendor. You should still review the vendor's current price, terms and privacy policy before
    making a purchase or creating an account.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">5. Questions</h2>
  <p>
    A verified public contact channel has not yet been configured. The disclosure and contact
    page will be updated before commercial advertising or visitor-submission features are
    enabled.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
